WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.493
Unit 2 is the answer: one record
for every provider's notice,

2
00:00:04.493 --> 00:00:10.325
called f m p provider notice, version
one, defined by a JSON schema in the kit.

3
00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:13.862
The notice I D is the provider
and the provider's own I D,

4
00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:16.675
and it's the key the
router de-duplicates on.

5
00:00:16.675 --> 00:00:20.787
The kind is one of the six, and
the status is open or closed.

6
00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:24.210
The window is the impact
window, always in U T C.

7
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:28.650
Services, regions and resources
are what the notice names.

8
00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:33.060
Then three fields that matter
most: whether action is required,

9
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.538
by when, and the action basis,
which says who said so.

10
00:00:36.538 --> 00:00:39.831
Either the provider said it,
in a field the record names,

11
00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:43.563
or a rule of the kit's inferred
it, and the record states the rule.

12
00:00:43.563 --> 00:00:46.612
First seen is when the
kit first read the notice.

13
00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:49.892
And the fingerprint is
a SHA-256 of the record

14
00:00:49.892 --> 00:00:53.349
without first seen and
the fingerprint itself.

15
00:00:53.349 --> 00:00:55.834
So a provider's edit
changes the fingerprint,

16
00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:58.788
and reading the same notice
again a week later doesn't.

17
00:00:58.788 --> 00:01:02.620
That's how the router tells a changed
notice from one it has already seen.
